			{
				"type": "Comment",
				"start": 0,
				"end": 531,
				"data": "\n\tA text run whose first word no longer fits after a predecessor that carries a FORCED break:\n\tthe whole run starts a fresh line and the boundary space is spent on that break, never\n\tre-emitted at the head of the continuation line. The boundary is the run's own fill `line`,\n\tmeasured from the predecessor's actual end column, so it hugs while the first word fits and\n\tmoves the run whole when it does not — the same answer for an inline element and an\n\texpression tag, and in the non-terminal and terminal positions alike.\n"
			},
			{
				"type": "Text",
				"start": 531,
				"end": 533,
